<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 1.19 million hectares with 1997/98 wheat by June 13, the Agriculture Secretariat said weekly crop report Friday.</p>
<p>Total wheat area should fall by between 7.5 percent and 13 percent from last season, said the Secretariat. It added that wheat sowing should fall in all provinces except the marginal area of Salta, where it should rise. Farmers have started sowing linseed in Entre Rios and Santa Fe. Rain in the week to June 13 mainly benefitted Buenos Aires, La Pampa and Santa Fe. Patchy rain fell in Cordoba but Entre Rios had none at all. Cordoba farms still need more soil moisture. </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Maize     3,926  100.0(100.0) 2,990.2   91.9  (88.2)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 6,280.9   98.7  (95.8)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,936.2  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sorghum     802  100.0(100.0)   689.5   94.5  (93.2)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   693.2   78.4  (72.6)</p>
